      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (California Public Employees\u2019 Retirement System)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We ask you to hold that American Pipe tolling applies to both of the time limits set forth in Section 13 of the Securities Act, which is reproduced in a number of places, including the blue brief at the top of page 3."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I don't want to interrupt you. We know American toll -- American Pipe applies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But the argument that you're making is the one that you describe, I think -- or am I correct, it's the one you say on page 38 of your brief is the easiest way to decide this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (California Public Employees\u2019 Retirement System)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is the argument that was presented straightforwardly in IndyMac, and it is simply the fact that under the text of Section 13, the class action complaint brought the action on our behalf."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Securities and civil procedure professors",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there is an amicus brief by securities and civil procedure professors who explain why it is that you haven't seen a ton of this yet"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Where -- where is the ambiguity in -- in no event?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, sir, if I could jut take you to the text, sir, because it's very rare that Congress just writes \"in no event.\" And so what it says is, in no event something. Okay? In no event, shall Alderson Reporting Company"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, what does the term \"such action\" mean?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we believe such action is an action that is otherwise subject to the discovery rule in the previous sentence. And that makes it make perfect sense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Class action practice in 1934 was quite different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Goldstein, could I ask you to speak to this question of your alternative theories, because in your briefing, the non-tolling theory, if I can call it that, took pride of place. But you haven't really spoken in those terms today. So what am I to make of that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 13 of the Securities Act, in its three-year time limit, plainly provides a statute of repose. This Court said as much in Lampf, and the two-tiered structure and emphatic, in-no-event language, admits of no other conclusion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "perhaps read beyond those particular words. And I think if you read beyond those words in the Clayton Act, you get a textual clue that this is a limitations period, because it says that it's subject to tolling if there is a government prosecution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I suppose one question is, what exactly do -- have we meant when we say a statute of repose? And we've certainly meant something different from a statute of limitations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, on at least two occasions, when this Court had a reason to label it one way or another, it -- this Court labeled the rule of American Pipe as the rule of equitable tolling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sure. A new complaint initiated with a, you know --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So what's an opt-out?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- could the judge have -- or can a judge, who has a class action and tells people, if you opt out, just file a motion to intervene?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is the action they're seeking to recover. That is the action to which you would apply the plain text of Section 13. And, I'm sorry, 2011 is too late under the plain terms of the statute, and it is a statute of repose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0002-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And it seems as though -- and tell me if you think this is wrong -- that the consequences go something like this: If we go your way in this case, any future suit like this, all large investors, the kind of investors CalPERS -- CalPERS is not going to make this mistake again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: You mean they're not worried about timeliness because they're relying on the class action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas C. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "equitable tolling or not matters much. This Court in\nWaldburger said the defining feature of a statute of\nrepose is they're not subject to tolling or estoppel.\nIt didn't use equitable tolling as a modifier. And, of\ncourse, as we've discussed, or as was discussed, if this\nrule is something other than a rule of equitable tolling\nand it's a legal rule, then the Rules Enabling Act\nproblem is front and center, because we have a defense\nunder Federal statutory law to substantive defense under\nWaldburger to not have new liability, new actions filed\nagainst us in over 3 years. If the only thing that\ntrumps that is a judicial construction of Rule 23,\nthere's a Rules Enabling Act problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas C. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At the end of the day, I think the path for\ndeciding this case is very clear. Section 13 is the\nstatute of repose. This Court said as much in Lampf.\nStatutes of repose are not subject to tolling. This\nCourt said as much in Waldburger. There's simply no\nbasis to deviate from this Court's precedence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas C. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is I don't believe that the statute\ncould be functioning as the Respondent suggests because\ntheir point is look, as the Petitioners see it, after\nthe class certification is denied or there's an opt-out\nperiod, then they'll have these individual lawsuits spin\nup and whoa, we didn't expect that at all.\nBut the world that they want is exactly the\nsame; it just involves more paperwork. What they want\nus to do is to intervene in the class action on day 1\nand then do nothing and sit back. And when we\neventually would otherwise intervene, then spin up our\nlawsuit. Nothing will have been gained. They won't be\non any more notice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas C. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do believe the other side\nprofoundly misunderstands the Private Securities\nLitigation Reform Act, the entire point of which was to\nnot have a bunch of parties in there litigating on their\nown. It doesn't contemplate that a bunch of\ninstitutional investors will be out there. It\ncontemplates that there will be one, and he's called the\nlead plaintiff.\nIt contemplates that other parties might try\nand become the lead plaintiff by submitting a notice,\nnot by moving to intervene. It contemplates that a new\nlead plaintiff could be named after the expiration of\nthree years"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas C. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-373",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "0491bd407aeba8c8774999fc40f424fcf86e5b9dfeb65e1d2fa6a0bde490bb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0491bd407aeb-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rule 23, then, says we want a representative\nparty. We don't want to take up the district judge's\ntime. That's the whole point of the rule.\nThe way you put those together is to say that the class\naction complaint, in the passive voice, brought the\naction on our behalf, and then we just took control of\nit when we opted out. Everything makes sense, and the\njudiciary, which is what's being protected here, not any\nequitable interest of us, but your district judges, all\ntheir interests are furthered together."
    },
    {
